{"hits": {"hits": [{"id": "28106", "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Qiu, Jian-wei"}, {"full_name": "Sterman, George F."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "353", "page_end": "136", "year": 1991, "page_start": "105", "journal_title": "Nucl.Phys.B"}], "texkeys": ["Qiu:1990xxa"], "imprints": [{"date": "1991"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "We review the leading 1/ Q 2 corrections to hadronic structure functions measured in deeply inelastic scattering, and we calculate the leading 1/ Q 2 corrections to Drell-Yan cross section. We find that the leading 1/ Q 2 corrections to a Drell-Yan cross section is given by the convolution of a calculable short-distance hard part, a twist-2 matrix element and a twist-4 matrix element. At leading order in \u03b1 s , the normalization of the 1/ Q 2 longitudinal structure functions for Drell-Yan cross sections are determined by higher-twist longitudinal structure functions in deeply inelastic scattering. Other experimental tests of 1/ Q 2 corrections are also discussed."}], "control_number": 28106, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0550-3213(91)90503-P"}], "titles": [{"title": "Power corrections in hadronic scattering. 1. Leading 1/Q**2 corrections to the Drell-Yan cross-section"}], "author_count": 2, "document_type": ["article"]}, "created": "1990-07-12T00:00:00+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/28106?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/28106?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/28106?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/28106?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/28106?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/28106?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A28106"}, "updated": "2023-03-07T03:51:30.920141+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Nuc